From 4afd0a374cfee920e13522e735eda55e71067ab9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 17:25:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bus: stm32_firewall: drop device links while detaching the
 node

When a peripheral cannot be accessed, the firewall detach its node
so it will not be probed.
But the device links supplier/consumers of the node are still in
place and the device link framework will issue an error when will
update such links due to the probe of a supplier or a provider of
the node.

	stm32-dbg-bus soc:bus@50080000: Failed to create device link (0x180) with supplier 50000000.rcc for /soc/bus@50080000/etm@500dc000

Drop the links supplier/consumers while detaching the node.

Signed-off-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: If58a7850b3014612bca280179bbe5df3f6eae280
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/573867
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 drivers/bus/stm32_firewall.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bus/stm32_firewall.c b/drivers/bus/stm32_firewall.c
index c9e6299197c3..4a8f5e9cff30 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/stm32_firewall.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/stm32_firewall.c
@@ -320,8 +320,11 @@ int stm32_firewall_populate_bus(struct stm32_firewall_controller *firewall_contr
 							      firewalls[i].firewall_id)) {
 				/*
 				 * Peripheral access not allowed or not defined.
-				 * Mark the node as populated so platform bus won't probe it
+				 * Mark the node as populated so platform bus won't probe it.
+				 * Drop the links supplier/consumers to prevent device link
+				 * to query the node.
 				 */
+				fwnode_links_purge(of_fwnode_handle(child));
 				of_detach_node(child);
 				dev_err(parent, "%s: Device driver will not be probed\n",
 					child->full_name);
-- 
